Optical fiber cables made up of individually sheathed fibers fall under heading 9001.10. This is a CBP ruling on flat drop toneable optical fiber cables. Heading 8544 covers insulated electric conductors, including optical fiber cables made up of individually sheathed fibers, whether or not assembled with electric conductors. Because the cable contains a copper conductor, it may be classified under 8544.70 (optical fiber cables). Subheading 8544.70.00 is the base, with the statistical suffix 8544.70.0000.

Heading 8544 includes "optical fiber cables, made up of individually sheathed fibers, whether or not containing electric conductors or assembled with connectors." Subheading 8544.70.00 has a 0% general rate, and the 10-digit code is 8544.70.0000.

{"hts_code": "8544.70.0000", "reason": "The cable is an optical fiber cable made up of individually sheathed (buffered) fibers combined with a copper conductor and without connectors, so it falls under heading 8544, subheading 8544.70."}
